public class Solution {
    public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
        if (n <= 0) {
            return false;
        }
        while (n % 3 == 0) {
            n /= 3;
        }
        return n == 1;
    }
}
```

This solution uses a while loop to repeatedly divide `n` by 3 until it becomes 1. If `n` becomes 1, then it means that `n` is a power of three, and the function returns true. Otherwise, it returns false.

The time complexity of this solution is O(log n), since we are dividing `n` by 3 in each iteration. The space complexity is O(1), since we are not using any extra space.

